          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"optionally formed like that of mas. nouns; so\u2013\u092e\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0924\u092f\u0947 or \u092e\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0928\u0947. See\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"Gr. \u00a769. P\u0101n. VII. I. 74.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Devanagari forms are not entirely clear.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"\u0938\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0928\u0941\u092d\u0942\u0924\u093f & \u2014\u0938\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0928\u0941\u092d\u0942\u0924\u093f\u2013self-perception, manifestation of Brahma\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"in contemplation. \u090f\u0915 means \u2018principal, chief\u2019, rather than \u2018sole\u2019;\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"cf. the couplet. \u090f\u0915\u094b\u093d\u0932\u094d\u092a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0925\u0947 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0927\u093e\u0928\u0947 \u091a &c. quoted in Gr. \u00a7 154; also\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"Amara \u2018 \u090f\u0915\u0947 \u092e\u0941\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0928\u094d\u092f\u0915\u0947\u0935\u0932\u093e\u0903 \u0964 \u092e\u093e\u0928\u2014\u092e\u0940\u092f\u0924\u0947\u093d\u0928\u0947\u0928\u0947\u0924\u093f \u092e\u093e\u0928\u092e\u094d from \u092e\u093e+\u0932\u094d\u092f\u0941\u091f\u094d\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"( \u0905\u0928 ), a measure; hence the means of arriving at correct\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"knowledge. In this sense the word \u092a\u094d\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923 is more common.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"The prama'nas, according to the Vedantins, are \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0915\u094d\u0937\u093e\u0928\u0941\u092e\u093e\u0928\u093e\u0917\u092e\u093e\u0903\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"\u092a\u094d\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u093e\u0928\u093f to which the Naiy\u00e1yikas add \u0909\u092a\u092e\u093e\u0928. Brahma is specially\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"regarded as \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0915\u094d\u0937\u092a\u094d\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0917\u092e\u094d\u092f \u2018capable of being realised by percep-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"tion,\u2019 although there are other means of knowing it such as\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":12,\"text\":\"\u0906\u0917\u092e &c. Another reading here is \u0938\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0928\u0941\u092d\u0942\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0947\u0915\u0938\u093e\u0930\u093e\u092f which Mr.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":13,\"text\":\"Telang interpretes in two ways:\u2013(1) to him who is the sole\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":14,\"text\":\"essence of self-knowledge; or (2) to him whose sole (or principal)\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":15,\"text\":\"essence is self-knowledge, preferring the former, as that, he\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":16,\"text\":\"thinks, gives the \u0905\u0926\u094d\u0935\u0948\u0924 view of the Veda'nta.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit words and transliteration marks are difficult to read.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"\u0936\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u093e\u092f &c.\u2014The dat. by \u0928\u092e\u0903\u0938\u094d\u0935\u0938\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0938\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0939\u093e\u0938\u094d\u0935\u0927\u093e\u0932\u0902\u0935\u0937\u0921\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0917\u093e\u091a\u094d\u091a\u2019 P\u0101n.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"II. 3. 16. \u0936\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0902 is one of the attributes of Brahma; cf. the S'ruti\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0928\u093f\u0937\u094d\u0915\u0932\u0902 \u0928\u093f\u0937\u094d\u0915\u094d\u0930\u093f\u092f\u0902 \u0936\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0902 \u0928\u093f\u0930\u0935\u0926\u094d\u092f\u0902 \u0928\u093f\u0930\u091e\u094d\u091c\u0928\u092e\u094d \u0964 \u2019 \u0924\u0947\u091c\u0938\u0947\u2013refers to Brahma and\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"not to the third element. Brahma is often called \u092a\u0930\u0902 \u091c\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0924\u093f\u0903 in\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"the Upanishads. Comp. \u090f\u0937 \u0938\u0902\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u093e\u0926\u0903.........\u092a\u0930\u0902 \u091c\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0924\u093f\u0930\u0941\u092a\u0938\u092e\u094d\u092a\u0926\u094d\u092f &c.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"Chh\u00e1ndogya; also the S'ruti \u0924\u0926\u0947\u0935 \u091c\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0924\u093f\u0937\u093e\u0902 \u091c\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0924\u093f\u0903 ( \u0909\u092a\u093e\u0938\u0924\u0947 ).\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"For the idea comp. Panchadas'\u00ee, quoted in the com.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit quotations and diacritics are indistinct.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"\u201cFor the idea may be compared Gregory Nyssen\u2019s description\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"of the divine nature quoted by the late Mr. Mansel in his philo-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"sophy of the Conditioned ( p. 16 ):\u2014It is neither in place nor\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"in time, but before these and above these in an unspeakable\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"manner, contemplated itself by itself through faith alone,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"neither measured by ages, nor moving along with times.\u201d\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r6\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 2. The present S'loka is said by the commentators\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"( whose remarks are perhaps based on a tradition which is almost\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"universal) to refer to a family intrigue the incidental discovery\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"of which filled Bhartr\u0325hari with disgust for worldly life. It is\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 2 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"1\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\",\"r3\",\"r4\",\"r5\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"2\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r6\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
        }
